This is a simple Python implementation of the Genetic Algorithm demonstration at www.ai-junkie.com
The original code was in C++. I felt the need of coding the thing myself, and decided to do it in Python.

The problem we solve is:
    "For any given 'target' number, find an expression invlolving any legal combination of 
    addition(+), subtraction(-), multiplication(*) and division(/) on digits that represents the 
    given target number.

    e.g., for the target 15, "9 + 3 * 2" is a solution."

    **Important: In Fup's code, the evaluation of the expressions generated was simple, left to right
    evaluation. I have used normal arithmetic precedence based evaluation(see `expr.py')


FX research scanner (fx_research/)
----------------------------------
The same GA idea applied to FX: every hour it labels each pair's last 7 trading
days with a regime, finds the most similar windows in the last 3 years, and
evolves fighter-entry settings (limit distance, SL/TP, re-pricing) on what
happened after them. Results go to the `fx_research` schema in Supabase.
See docs/FX_MT4_PLAN.md for how it ties into MT4-TradeSignals and TradeCoreV2.

    pip install -r requirements.txt
    python -m fx_research.scan --dry-run
    python -m fx_research.scheduler
